{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T12:01:31.626117Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nHere's the plan for your new **business round trip** (same dates, same 3 passengers, no baggage, no insurance):\n\n**Flights (cheapest business options for your dates):**\n- **Outbound (2024-05-26):** HAT023, JFK → SFO (direct) — **$364**\n- **Return (2024-05-28):** HAT204, SFO → SEA, then HAT100, SEA → JFK — **$248 + $259 = $507**\n\n**Total:** $871 per passenger × 3 = **$2,613**\n\n**Payment breakdown (maximizing certificates, then gift cards):**\n- Certificate (only **one** can be used per reservation, so I'll use your largest): **$500** (certificate_3765853)\n- Gift cards (both): $198 + $129 = **$327**\n- **Mastercard: $2,613 − $500 − $327 = $1,786**\n\nYour other two certificates ($250 each) will remain in your account.\n\n**A note on the refund:** Canceling your current reservation refunds the **$567** to your gift card (gift_card_6136092), but that takes **5–7 business days**, so it won't be available for this new booking right away. If you'd prefer to **wait for the refund** before booking, your Mastercard charge would drop to **$1,219** instead of $1,786.\n\n**Comparison:** If you instead just changed the cabin of your existing reservation to business (keeping the same flights), the Mastercard charge would be **$1,801**. So **canceling and rebooking is slightly cheaper** for your Mastercard ($1,786 vs. $1,801).\n\nBefore I proceed, please confirm:\n1. **Cancellation reason** — I understand it's a *change of plan* (rebooking in business). Is that correct?\n2. Do you want to **proceed now** (Mastercard $1,786), or **wait for the refund** first (Mastercard $1,219)?"}, "resultat": "Thank you for breaking that down.\n\nI'd like to proceed now. However, I have an idea to use all three certificates. We can book three separate reservations. I'll use the $500 certificate and all gift cards for my reservation. Then, we can use certificate_9984806 for Aarav's reservation, and the other certificate for Evelyn's reservation. We can then pay the rest with my Mastercard.\n\nAt the end of the day, I want to know how much my Mastercard will be charged in total for all three reservations.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-13T12:02:41.407641Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "\n\nGreat idea! Let me lay out the plan for **three separate business reservations** (same flights, same dates, 1 passenger each):\n\n**Flights (same for all three):**\n- Outbound (2024-05-26): HAT023, JFK → SFO — $364\n- Return (2024-05-28): HAT204, SFO → SEA — $248; HAT100, SEA → JFK — $259\n- **Total per passenger: $871**\n\n**Payment breakdown:**\n\n| Passenger | Certificate | Gift Cards | Mastercard |\n|-----------|------------|------------|------------|\n| Mohamed | $500 (cert_3765853) | $198 + $129 = $327 | **$44** |\n| Aarav | $250 (cert_9984806) | — | **$621** |\n| Evelyn | $250 (cert_2765295) | — | **$621** |\n\n**Total Mastercard charge: $44 + $621 + $621 = $1,286**\n\nBefore I proceed, I need a few things:\n\n1. **Passenger details:** I have Mohamed's info, but I don't have records for **Aarav** or **Evelyn**. Could you provide their **last names** and **dates of birth** (YYYY-MM-DD)?\n2. **Cancellation confirmation:** I'll cancel reservation K1NW8N with the reason **\"change of plan\"** (rebooking in business). Is that correct?\n\nOnce I have those details, I'll confirm everything with you before making any changes."}, "resultat": "That's an excellent plan!\n\nFor Aarav, the last name is Silva, and the date of birth is 2010-06-15.\nFor Evelyn, the last name is Silva, and the date of birth is 2012-09-22.\n\nYes, please cancel reservation K1NW8N with the reason \"change of plan.\"\n\nI'm ready when you are.", "erreur": null}
